menu "SempreIoT heat and humidity sensing (siot_sensing)"

    config SIOT_FEATURE_SENSING
        bool "Heat and humidity rules on this unit (protocol section 7.1.6)"
        default n
        help
            Samples the unit's temperature / humidity sensor once per second
            and raises HEAT_ALARM (57.0 C), HEAT_RISE_ALARM (8.0 C in 60 s),
            SENSOR_WET (99.7 %) and SENSOR_FAULT; fills TEMP / HUMIDITY in the
            unit's EVENT and HEARTBEAT. Does nothing on a model whose pin map
            has no sensor bus. Every number:
            docs/phases-development/phase5-heat-humidity-sensing-brief.md
            section 4. Node image; the battery unit's side is not written yet.

    config SIOT_SENSING_DTR_TEST
        bool "Bench: exercise the sensor's interrupt pin on a unit that is awake"
        depends on SIOT_FEATURE_SENSING
        default n
        help
            The DTR test, part A (brief section 10.1): every 60 s the
            temperature threshold of the sensor is re-armed at the current
            reading + 4.0 C (what a battery unit does at each wake), and every
            change of the interrupt pin is logged with the status register.
            Off: the threshold stays at 57 C. Detection on a mains unit never
            depends on the pin either way.

endmenu
